course: dictionary
lesson: 7609
title: Prismatic: shapes, light and rainbows
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These are its context. «Some microbes live in extreme places, such as boiling hot springs; the bright rings of Grand Prismatic Spring in Yellowstone are mats of different microbes living at different temperatures.» The clue is «bright rings», and the spring's name has prismatic in it, so the word probably describes something shining with many colours.
explain: The same word can have different meanings. «Prismatic colours» means bright colours shining like a rainbow. «A prismatic compass» means a compass that uses a prism. Look at the word after prismatic to find out which meaning fits. In maths lessons it describes shapes, and in science it describes light.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence. Try «the bright rings are shining with many colours». Does it still make sense? If yes, you have probably got it right.
fact: Prismatic means shaped like a prism, which is a solid with two matching ends and flat sides.
fact: Prismatic can also mean splitting white light into the colours of the rainbow, as a glass prism does.
fact: «Prismatic colours» are many bright colours shining together.
fact: «Prismatic crystals» are crystals that shine with many colours.
fact: Grand Prismatic Spring in Yellowstone is named for its bright, many-coloured rings.
exercise: The bright rings of «Grand Prismatic Spring» shine with many colours. What does prismatic suggest here? | Very cold to touch | *Shining with many colours, like a rainbow | Shaped like a cardboard box | Dull and grey
exercise: Maya says a Toblerone box is prismatic. What does prismatic mean in this case? | Using a prism to measure angles | Round, like a ball | Shining with rainbow colours | *Shaped like a prism, with two matching ends and flat sides
exercise: Which phrase describes a compass that uses a prism? | Prismatic colours | Prismatic springs | *Prismatic compass | Prismatic crystals
test: What does a glass prism do to white light? | Makes it disappear completely | Makes it heavier | *Splits it into the colours of the rainbow | Turns it into sound
test: «Prismatic crystals» sparkled in the cave. Which word is closest in meaning? | Heavy | Silent | Dull | *Shining with many colours
exam: Which of these is a prismatic shape? | A bicycle wheel | A flat pancake | A football | *A Toblerone box
